# Example requests. In VS Code, install the "REST Client" extension
# and click "Send Request" above each one. Start the API first with: npm run dev

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Is the process alive? (liveness, doesn't touch the database)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Can it serve requests? (readiness, checks the database: 200 or 503)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Create a restaurant (201). The code is saved in uppercase.
POST {{baseUrl}}/restaurants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "camden",
  "name": "Nando's Camden",
  "city": "London"
}

### Create another one, in a different city
POST {{baseUrl}}/restaurants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "MCR-PICCADILLY",
  "name": "Nando's Piccadilly",
  "city": "Manchester"
}

### Same code again (409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/restaurants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "CAMDEN",
  "name": "Another Camden",
  "city": "London"
}

### Invalid body (400, with the fields that are wrong)
POST {{baseUrl}}/restaurants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "!",
  "name": ""
}

### List restaurants: the first page, 20 by default (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/restaurants

### List restaurants in one city, 10 per page, second page (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/restaurants?city=London&limit=10&offset=10

### A limit over 100 (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/restaurants?limit=1000

### Send your own request id: it comes back in the X-Request-Id header and appears in the logs
GET {{baseUrl}}/restaurants
X-Request-Id: my-test-request-1

### Get one restaurant. Paste an id from the responses above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/restaurants/PASTE-AN-ID-HERE

### Deactivate it (200). Only name, city and isActive can change.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/restaurants/PASTE-AN-ID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isActive": false
}

### Delete it (204). If it's still active you get a 409.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/restaurants/PASTE-AN-ID-HERE
